llowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T21:27:34Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T21:29:22Z","body":"I played around with this a bit on 4.7. The MRP uses the default velocity direction (1,0,0) and spread (45.0). With these two set to (0,0,0) and 0.0 it looks ok to me (i.e. particles going out along sphere's surface normals).\n\nRegenerating \"Create Emission Points from Node\" -> \"Surface Points + Normal (Directed)\" generates both point and normal textures.\n\nNot sure what's supposed to happen when you have both a normal direction and a velocity direction. I suppose I'd expect them to be added (then maybe normalized), though that's not what's happening.\n\nvelocity direction -> observed movement\n\n1,0,0 -> swirls around Z\n0,1,0 -> flows towards -Z\n0,0,1 -> no change; same as 0,0,0; moves along normal\n\nWith @Kaleb-Reid changes \n\n1,0,0 -> swirls around Y\n0,1,0 -> flows towards Y\n0,0,1 -> no change; same as 0,0,0; moves along normal\n\n🤷\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3899579628/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133782369","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100846#issuecomment-4133782369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100846","id":4133782369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72ZINh","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T11:21:59Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T11:21:59Z","body":"After fixing the normals generation, i feel like the current implementation is working as intended: normals are on the Z axis. What could be done is to hide the \"direction\" property and leave only spread, which i feel like would make sense in this case. Thoughts?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133782369/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]